The '''2025–26 La Liga''', also known as '''La Liga EA Sports'''<ref>{{cite news |title=EA SPORTS & LaLiga Announce Expansive New Partnership With EA SPORTS FC as Title Sponsor of All LaLiga Competitions |url=https://news.ea.com/press-releases/press-releases-details/2022/EA-SPORTS--LaLiga-Announce-Expansive-New-Partnership-With-EA-SPORTS-FC-as-Title-Sponsor-of-All-LaLiga-Competitions/default.aspx |publisher=Electronic Arts |date=2 August 2022 |access-date=27 April 2023 |archive-date=2 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220802132511/https://news.ea.com/press-releases/press-releases-details/2022/EA-SPORTS--LaLiga-Announce-Expansive-New-Partnership-With-EA-SPORTS-FC-as-Title-Sponsor-of-All-LaLiga-Competitions/default.aspx |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=EA SPORTS FC will be the title sponsor of all LaLiga competitions |url=https://www.laliga.com/en-GB/news/ea-sports-fc-will-be-the-title-sponsor-of-all-laliga-competitions |publisher=La Liga |date=2 August 2022 |access-date=14 May 2023 |archive-date=2 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220802132606/https://www.laliga.com/en-GB/news/ea-sports-fc-will-be-the-title-sponsor-of-all-laliga-competitions |url-status=live }}</ref> due to sponsorship reasons, was the 95th season of [[La Liga]], Spain's top-flight football competition. It began on 15 August 2025 and ended on 24 May 2026. The match schedule was published on 1 July 2025.<ref>{{cite news|title=Countdown to league fixtures for 2025/26|url=https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/4299175/countdown-to-league-fixtures-for-202526/featured|website=FC Barcelona|date=30 June 2025|access-date=28 August 2025|archive-date=14 August 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250814105941/https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/4299175/countdown-to-league-fixtures-for-202526/featured|url-status=live}}</ref> [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] were the defending champions, having won their 28th title the previous season.

On 10 May 2026, [[2025–26 FC Barcelona season|Barcelona]] officially secured their second consecutive title with three matches to spare following a 2–0 win against [[El Clásico]] rivals [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c78qwgnn3vgt|title=Barcelona 2 Real Madrid 0|date=10 May 2026|work=BBC Sport|access-date=11 May 2026|archive-date=10 May 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260510222900/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c78qwgnn3vgt|url-status=live}}</ref>

