===Promotion and relegation (pre-season)===
A total of twenty teams contested the league, including seventeen sides from the [[2024–25 La Liga|2024–25 season]] and three promoted from the [[2024–25 Segunda División]]. This included the two top teams from the Segunda División, and the winners of the [[2025 Segunda División play-offs|promotion play-offs]].

;Teams relegated to Segunda División
The first team to be relegated from La Liga were [[Real Valladolid|Valladolid]], after a 1–5 loss to [[Real Betis]] on 25 April 2025, after only a single season stay in the top tier. The second team to be relegated was [[UD Las Palmas|Las Palmas]], after a 0–1 loss to [[Sevilla FC|Sevilla]] on 14 May 2025, after two seasons in the top tier. The third and final team relegated to Segunda was [[CD Leganés|Leganés]], after just one season in the top tier, after [[RCD Espanyol|Espanyol]] managed to survive by beating Las Palmas on the last matchday.
;Teams promoted from Segunda División
On 25 May 2025, [[Levante UD|Levante]] became the first side to be promoted, returning after a three-year absence following a 3–2 victory against [[Burgos CF|Burgos]]. [[Elche CF|Elche]] became the second team to be promoted on the last day after defeating [[Deportivo de La Coruña|Deportivo La Coruña]] 4–0, returning after a two-year absence. The final team promoted was [[Real Oviedo|Oviedo]] after overcoming [[CD Mirandes|Mirandés]] 3–2 on aggregate in the promotion play-off final on 21 June to return to the top division after a twenty four-year absence.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c74wx8ykpggo |title=Cazorla scores as Real Oviedo return to La Liga |publisher=BBC Sport |date=21 June 2025 |access-date=21 June 2025 |archive-date=5 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250805025847/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c74wx8ykpggo |url-status=live }}</ref>

